<h2>Data, attribution, and responsible use</h2>
<p>FreeOpenOcean surfaces open map and photomap contributions with on-map attribution (for example OpenStreetMap-related credits where applicable). Always treat chart layers as decision-support context: verify critical navigation with official publications, Notices to Mariners, and local knowledge. Weather, depth, and hazards change; a beautiful map is not a substitute for seamanship.</p>
<p>We aim for clarity in sourcing and UI so you can see <em>what</em> you are looking at and <em>why</em> it is shown. That transparency is part of making open ocean charts genuinely useful—not just decorative.</p>

